---
# The keys of the vault, group_vars/all/local.vault.yml (git-ignored): Ansible's secrets, encrypted with the
# password in .vault_pass. make vault TYPE=new makes an empty vault and a .vault_pass when there are none, and
# make vault opens it to add a key. Neither file is ever committed: keep a copy of both in your password
# manager (README.md, The vault). Only the keys a setup uses are needed, and none is set here.
#
# With a NAS: the TrueNAS API key, for a local user in builtin_administrators, made in its web UI over HTTPS
# (scripts/runbooks/REBUILD.md, section 2).
# vault_truenas_api_key: <the key>
#
# With alert mail (truenas_mail_server in local.yml): the mail server's password.
# vault_truenas_mail_password: <the password>
#
# With remote access (tailscale_advertise_routes in local.yml): a one-off, pre-approved auth key, tagged
# tag:homeserver, spent at the host's first login (scripts/runbooks/tailscale.md, section 4).
# vault_tailscale_auth_key: <the key>
#
# With Home Assistant (haos_mac in local.yml): the password of its owner account, which homeassistant.yml creates
# before anyone else on the network can; 12 characters at least.
# vault_haos_owner_password: <the password>
